{"text": "To reach the target of 24 using the numbers 6, 10, 10, and 13 with each number used exactly once and by using the basic arithmetic operations (+, -, *, /), we can approach this problem by trying out different combinations of operations.", "start": 0, "end": 236, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "One possible solution is:", "start": 238, "end": 263, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 - 6) × (13 - 10) = 4 × 3 = 12", "start": 265, "end": 298, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "This does not give us 24 yet.", "start": 300, "end": 329, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's try other combinations:", "start": 330, "end": 359, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "((13 - 6) × 10) div 10 = 7 × 10 div 10 = 70 div 10 = 7", "start": 361, "end": 415, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Still not 24.", "start": 417, "end": 430, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's keep trying:", "start": 431, "end": 449, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "(13 - 10) × (10 - 6) = 3 × 4 = 12", "start": 451, "end": 484, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Again, not 24.", "start": 486, "end": 500, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's try another combination:", "start": 501, "end": 531, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "(10 × 13) - (10 + 6) = 130 - 16 = 114", "start": 533, "end": 570, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "This is still not it.", "start": 572, "end": 593, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's consider a more complex approach:", "start": 594, "end": 633, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "(10 × (13 - 10)) + 6 = 10 × 3 + 6 = 30 + 6 = 36", "start": 635, "end": 682, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "This is also not what we need.", "start": 684, "end": 714, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's try:", "start": 715, "end": 725, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "(13 + 10) × (10 div 6) = 23 × (10/6) = (230/6) approx 38.33", "start": 727, "end": 786, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not helpful.", "start": 788, "end": 800, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's go back to simpler operations:", "start": 801, "end": 837, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "10 + 10 + 13 - 6 = 37", "start": 839, "end": 860, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 + 10 + 6 + 13 = 49", "start": 862, "end": 883, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "We need to think of a combination where we use division or other operations differently.", "start": 885, "end": 973, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Consider:", "start": 974, "end": 983, "label": "request"}
{"text": "10 × (13 - 6) - 10 = 10 × 7 - 10 = 70 - 10 = 60", "start": 985, "end": 1032, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Finally, the correct combination is:", "start": 1034, "end": 1070, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 + 10) - (10 - 6) = 23 - (-4) = 23 + 4 = 24", "start": 1072, "end": 1118, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So the correct solution is:", "start": 1120, "end": 1147, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 + 10) - (10 - 6) = 24", "start": 1149, "end": 1174, "label": "inform"}
